# FM92RS-only names and notes (hand-written; portann.py appends this file to FM92RS.ann)
=1145 selcall_decode_task
=11e3 selcall_decode_reset
=12fc tone_chip_reset
=1309 selcall_call_received
=150b selcall_timeout_task
1145 RS selcall decoder (inferred): loads the expected digit of the own code ($D5,x) into the tone chip, waits for $80 bit7, digit windows from 1F84
1167 next digit: $BE = digits left (from 1F7A), $C0 = index; same digit as previous -> repeat tone ($0A/$0B)
118e all digits matched: hold-off from 1F84 into $E7, then $A3 bit0 = call received
11e3 called from tx_stop: re-arm the decoder (only if selcall decode enabled: $32 bit1, $34 bit7)
11f5 1F7A = number of digits in the own code
12f7 RS: low nibble (tone number) inverted before the write to $80
12fc RS tone chip reset: $84 = $7F, then strobe $80 bit4
1322 1FB6 -> $EF (1 s soft timer): selcall timeout, read only by FM92RS
0b07 RS: $EA-$EC every 64 ticks (FM92R: $E9,$EA)
0b22 RS: $ED-$EF every 2304 ticks (FM92R: $EB,$EC)
099c RS: extra fast timer $E9 (FM92R: $E7,$E8 only)
10fe 1FB4 = vote/scan dwell time
150b RS: when $EF runs out, clears the selcall state and calls sub_13d8 (inferred: auto-reset of a received call)
15f3 RS: $80 = $50 at start-up (FM92R: $00)
15ff RS: tone chip set-up $84 = $7F, also kept in $A4 (FM92R: $B0)
1309 runs when a decode has finished ($A3 bit4 set, bit2 clear) and selcall decode is enabled
131d tell the head a call was received ($A7) (inferred)
1358 alert: $80 bit5 on, $ED = $11 (~17 s) (inferred)
134b $15 bit5 starts selcall_encode_task on the main loop: automatic reply/transpond (inferred)
=1275 selcall_send_start
0aee soft timers: $57-$61,$EA-$EC every 64 ticks (~27 ms)
0b14 $63-$65,$ED-$EF every 2304 ticks (~1 s)
1275 RS: the tone-chip reset is now a call (FM92R: inline $84 = $B0, tone 15)
